---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Spotting the 'Slaughterhouse': 2026 Phishing Spreadsheet Scams | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="Security alert exposing the 'Dashen' redirect traps, fake 'Login Walls', and malicious spreadsheet hubs designed to steal Kakobuy credentials and wallet balances."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Spotting the 'Slaughterhouse': Identifying phishing spreadsheet sites in 2026"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="18 May 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'spreadsheet phishing scams',
    'fake Kakobuy links',
    'dashenseo scam redirect',
    'protecting agent account',
    'reps security alert 2026',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    This guide supports shoppers on the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> directory at kakobuy-cn.com. In the world of reps, a "Slaughterhouse" (杀猪盘) isn't just a metaphor—it's a multi-million dollar industry. In 2026, scammers have moved beyond simple fake links to building entire <strong>phishing spreadsheet ecosystems</strong>. These sites look identical to community favorites but are engineered to hijack your session and drain your Kakobuy wallet.
  </p>

  <h2>The "Dashen" Redirect Trap</h2>
  <p>
    The most common scam in 2026 involves using high-authority domains like Google Sites (e.g., <code>sites.google.com/view/...</code>) to host a "Best Finds" list. When you click a product link, you are silently bounced through a series of malicious redirects, often involving <code>daohang3.dashenseo.cc</code> or similar domains.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The Goal:</strong> These redirects attempt to capture your <strong>Browser Cookies</strong>. If successful, the scammer can "clone" your logged-in session on Kakobuy without ever needing your password.
  </p>

  <h2>Three Red Flags of a 2026 Scam Site</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>The "Login Wall":</strong> If a spreadsheet asks you to "Connect your Kakobuy account" or "Sign in to see QC photos," <strong>LEAVE IMMEDIATELY.</strong> Real spreadsheets like ours never require your agent credentials.</li>
    <li><strong>The "VPN/Human Verification" Pop-up:</strong> Scammers often force you to click a "Verify you are human" button that actually installs a malicious browser extension or triggers a cookie-theft script.</li>
    <li><strong>Suspicious Domain Suffixes:</strong> Be wary of sites ending in <code>.top</code>, <code>.cc</code>, <code>.xyz</code>, or <code>.win</code> that claim to be "Official Kakobuy Partners." Kakobuy does not have official partners outside its verified social channels.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Anatomy of a Safe vs. Malicious Link</h2>
  <div class="blog-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Feature</th>
          <th>Safe Link (e.g. kakobuy-cn.com)</th>
          <th>Scam Link (e.g. dashenseo)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Direct Target</td>
          <td><code>https://weidian.com/...</code></td>
          <td><code>https://daohang.xxx.cc/jump?url=...</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Intermediate Bounces</td>
          <td>Zero</td>
          <td>3 to 5 hidden redirects</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Data Requested</td>
          <td>None</td>
          <td>Session Cookies / Login Tokens</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>How to Protect Your Account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enable 2FA:</strong> Two-Factor Authentication is your only defense if your cookies are stolen. Enable it now in your Kakobuy security settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the URL:</strong> Always verify you are on <code>kakobuy-cn.com</code> or the official <code>kakobuy.com</code> before interacting with any sensitive data.</li>
    <li><strong>Report Abuse:</strong> If you find a scam site hosted on Google Sites, use the "Report Abuse" button at the bottom. This helps the community take down these "Slaughterhouses."</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <strong>Stay Vigilant:</strong> For more on safe sharing habits, read our <a href="/blog/google-sheets-sharing-spreadsheet-curator-opsec/">Google Sheets opsec guide</a>.
  </p>
</BlogArticleShell>
